    "text": "# Engineering Handbook: Incident Response for HydroCore Control Systems (HCCS)\n\n**Document ID:** HCCS-IR-2024-01\n**Version:** 3.2\n**Classification:** Internal Engineering Use Only\n**Applicability:** All HydroCore Control Service (HCCS) Field Engineers, SCADA Administrators, and Incident Commanders.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Introduction and Scope\n\n### 1.1 Purpose\nThis handbook defines the standardized procedures for detecting, analyzing, containing, and recovering from incidents affecting the HydroCore Control Service (HCCS). HCCS manages the Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) systems for municipal water treatment plants, including chemical dosing, filtration backwashing, and pump station automation.\n\n### 1.2 Criticality Levels\nIncidents are classified based on impact to public health, environmental safety, and operational continuity.\n\n| Level | Designation | Definition | Response Time |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P1** | **Critical** | Immediate threat to public health (e.g., chlorine under-dosing, turbidity spikes >5 NTU) or total loss of control. | <",
